==Finnish==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|fi|ǵneh₃}}
From {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*koneh}}, from Pre-Finnic ''*konïš'', borrowed from Pre-{{der|fi|gem}} ''*gn̥ni̯o-'' (later {{cog|gem-pro|*kunją||omen, portent, miracle}}), from {{der|fi|ine-pro|*ǵneh₃-}}. Cognates include {{cog|non|kyn||wonder}}. The original meaning in Finnish was ''magic'', from  which only recently ''machine''.<ref>Kallio, Petri: [http://www.sgr.fi/sust/sust266/sust266_kallio.pdf The Prehistoric Germanic Loanword Strata in Finnic]</ref> Compare with {{cog|krl|koneh||magic}} and {{m|krl|konehtie||to conjure}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fi-IPA|*}}
* {{rhymes|e|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|ko|ne|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[machine]]
# [[appliance]] {{gloss|apparatus or device, typically powered electrically, used in homes to perform domestic functions}}
#: ''[[kodinkone|kodin'''kone''']], [[kotitalouskone|kotitalous'''kone''']]'' -- [[household appliance|household '''appliance''']]
# {{short for|lang=fi|lentokone||airplane}}

